<title>USA: PS Colo. plans to start 262 MW unit Tues.</title>
<headline>PS Colo. plans to start 262 MW unit Tues.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public Service Co of Colorado plans to restart the 262 megawatt (MW) unit 2 at the Hayden power station on Tuesday, a company spokeswoman confirmed Friday.</p>
<p>As previously reported, the Steamboat Springs, Colo., unit was shut at 2400 MDT Thursday for scheduled maintenance.</p>
<p>The Hayden plant's 180 MW unit 1 is operating normally, the utility said.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau, + 1 213 955 6761</p>
